# Requirements Rule

## When This Applies
When the agent is starting a new feature, bug fix, or enhancement task and needs to gather requirements.

## Integration Configuration
Always read `config/integrations.yaml` first. This file controls:
- Which issue tracker to use (Jira / GitHub Issues / Linear)
- Whether Figma is enabled and what to extract
- Which external URL routes to which MCP
- Whether to fetch attachments and linked URLs

## Requirements Sources (process ALL of these, in this order)

### 1. Issue Tracker (Jira / GitHub Issues / Linear)
Fetch the ticket and extract EVERY piece of content:
- Full description (not a summary — the entire text)
- Acceptance criteria (custom field or parsed from description)
- **Remote Links / Web Links** — all explicitly added external URLs
- **Attachments** — every file uploaded to the ticket
- **Comments** — full thread for additional context
- Linked tickets (parent epic, blockers, relates-to)

### 2. Figma Design Links (MANDATORY if present)
**Detect** Figma URLs in: description, web links, comments, any field.
Figma URL patterns: `figma.com/file/`, `figma.com/design/`, `figma.com/proto/`

**If found AND `config/integrations.yaml > design.figma.enabled = true`:**
Extract using `agentic-pdlc-framework/skills/figma-integration.md`:
- ✅ Frame export as image (embed in requirements)
- ✅ All UI components with variants/states
- ✅ Every text string: labels, placeholders, error messages, button text (exact strings)
- ✅ Color tokens and typography styles used
- ✅ Spacing/layout values
- ✅ All prototype interactions (trigger → action → destination)
- ✅ Responsive variants (mobile, tablet if present)
- ✅ Designer annotations (unresolved comments on the frame)

Each text string → Functional Requirement
Each interaction → Acceptance Criterion

**If found but Figma NOT configured:**
Flag: `⚠️ DESIGN GAP: Figma link found but MCP not configured — configure in config/integrations.yaml`
Ask user: "A Figma design is linked. Shall I proceed without it, or can you set up Figma access?"

### 3. Other External URLs and Attachments
Process ALL sources using `agentic-pdlc-framework/skills/external-sources.md`:

| Source Type | Handler | What to Extract |
|------------|---------|-----------------|
| Confluence page links | Confluence MCP | Full page content, summarize relevant sections |
| Linked Jira tickets | Jira MCP | Summary, status, ACs — used as dependency context |
| GitHub issue/PR links | GitHub MCP | What was the issue, how was it resolved |
| Image attachments (jpg/png/gif) | Vision | Describe: layout, components, state, data shown |
| PDF attachments | Text extraction | Spec tables, requirement lists, API contracts |
| Text/Markdown attachments | Read directly | All content |
| Other URLs (public) | HTTP fetch | Page title + main content summary |

**Never skip attachments or remote links.** They often contain the real specification.

### 4. Git Context
- Recent commits on files related to this feature area
- Open PRs touching the same code paths

### 5. Local Documentation
- `docs/` folder for existing specs and ADRs
- `README.md` for project-level constraints
- `config/project.yaml` for tech stack and coding standards

### 6. Direct User Prompt
Treat any constraints or details the user provides as highest-priority override.

